From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: propagate platform reset failure in cdns_role_set()

cdns_role_set() resets the CDNSP controller before activating a new
Type-C role but previously ignored the return value of
cdnsp_platform_reset():

	if (role != USB_ROLE_NONE)
		cdnsp_platform_reset(cdns->dev);

	ret = cdns_role_start(cdns, role);

This allowed cdns_role_start() to run - and xHCI to be started - after
a failed reset, failed clock operation, or failed reset deassertion,
leaving the controller in an undefined state. Propagate the error and
bail out before starting the new role, matching the equivalent fix
already applied to the resume path.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c
@@ -402,8 +402,15 @@ static int cdns_role_set(struct usb_role_switch *sw, enum usb_role role)
 	 * This is critical for Type-C hotplug where orientation flip needs
 	 * to be re-applied to PHY registers.
 	 */
-	if (role != USB_ROLE_NONE)
-		cdnsp_platform_reset(cdns->dev);
+	if (role != USB_ROLE_NONE) {
+		ret = cdnsp_platform_reset(cdns->dev);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(cdns->dev,
+				"platform reset failed before role %d start: %d\n",
+				role, ret);
+			goto pm_put;
+		}
+	}
 
 	ret = cdns_role_start(cdns, role);
 	if (ret)
